.Dd October 6, 2026
.Dt BHOTKEYS-START 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm bhotkeys-start
.Nd start bhotkeys for an X session
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl Fl no-bosd
.Op Ar manager
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the one line a session script needs to bring up
.Xr bhotkeys 1 .
It does three things, in order.
.Bl -enum
.It
Runs
.Xr bosd-start 1
when it is on
.Ev PATH ,
so the plugins that paint a gauge or a caption find a daemon.
.Fl Fl no-bosd
skips this step, for a session whose plugins do not use
.Xr bosd 1
or where something else starts it.
A failure here is reported by
.Nm bosd-start
and does not stop the rest.
.It
Starts the session listener,
.Nm bhotkeys Fl Fl daemon ,
in the background.
With
.Ar manager ,
the listener is told
.Fl Fl wm Ar manager
and does not wait to detect one.
Without it, the listener detects the manager itself, waiting up
to 30 seconds for one it knows.
.It
Runs that manager's apply script,
.Pa @PREFIX@/libexec/bhotkeys/bhotkeys- Ns Ar manager Ns Pa -apply ,
in the background with
.Fl Fl wait .
With
.Ar manager ,
the name is the argument.
Without it,
.Nm bhotkeys Fl Fl print-wm
waits up to 30 seconds for a manager the listener knows,
and that name selects the script.
A manager already running is found on the first scan.
The script polls for the manager once a second for up to 30 seconds,
then registers the listener's chords with it so the focused client
does not see them.
A manager with no apply script is simply not applied.
.El
.Pp
.Ar manager
is a name
.Xr bhotkeys 1
accepts for
.Fl Fl wm .
.Pp
The listener keeps one instance per user.
When one is already running,
.Nm
leaves it alone and the new one exits.
.Nm bhotkeys
is taken from the directory
.Nm
runs from when it is there, and from
.Ev PATH
otherwise.
The apply script is taken from that same directory when it is
there, and from
.Pa @PREFIX@/libexec/bhotkeys
otherwise.
.Pp
A
.Pa ~/.xsession
for MATE:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
if [ ! "$DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS" ]; then
	eval "$( dbus-launch --sh-syntax --exit-with-session )"
fi
exec mate-session
.Ed
.Pp
The bus lines stay in the session script.
A child cannot export the address into the shell that runs the
session, and the apply scripts for the GNOME family need it.
.Pp
GNOME, KDE, LXDE, LXQt, MATE, X-Cinnamon, and XFCE start
.Nm
from
.Pa @PREFIX@/etc/xdg/autostart/bhotkeys.desktop
when the session starts.
That entry does not name a manager.
The listener detects one, and the apply script for that name runs.
.Pp
i3 does not read that directory.
Include
.Pa @PREFIX@/share/bhotkeys/i3.conf
from the i3 config:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
include @PREFIX@/share/bhotkeys/i3.conf
.Ed
.Pp
.Cm bvwm ,
.Cm dwm ,
.Cm fluxbox ,
.Cm fvwm ,
.Cm openbox ,
.Cm windowmaker ,
and
.Cm xmonad
do not read that directory.
.Cm fvwm
is the name for the fvwm and fvwm3 programs.
.Pp
XDM runs
.Pa ~/.xsession
as the session.
Name the manager, then replace the shell with the window manager:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
bhotkeys-start dwm
exec dwm
.Ed
.Pp
GDM and SDDM source
.Pa ~/.xprofile
and then run the session selected in the menu.
Put the start line there:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
bhotkeys-start dwm
.Ed
.Pp
SDDM also sources
.Pa ~/.xsession
before the selected session.
An
.Ic exec
of the window manager in that file replaces the session SDDM was
given.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "DISPLAY"
.It Ev DISPLAY
X server to watch.
The default is
.Pa :0 .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "@PREFIX@/etc/xdg/autostart/bhotkeys.desktop" -compact
.It Pa @PREFIX@/libexec/bhotkeys/
The apply scripts.
.It Pa @PREFIX@/etc/xdg/autostart/bhotkeys.desktop
Starts
.Nm
for GNOME, KDE, LXDE, LXQt, MATE, X-Cinnamon, and XFCE.
.It Pa @PREFIX@/share/bhotkeys/i3.conf
i3 config to include.
Runs
.Nm i3 .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 1 when
.Nm bhotkeys
is not found or the arguments are wrong, and 0 otherwise.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bhotkeys 1 ,
.Xr bhotkeys-greeter 1 ,
.Xr bosd 1 ,
.Xr bosd-start 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Devin Teske Aq Mt dteske@FreeBSD.org
